$(g \circ f)(x) = g(f(x)) = g(\ln x) = 3 + \ln x$
$g \circ f$ is $y = 3 + \ln x$
$(g \circ f)^{-1}$ is $x = 3 + \ln y \implies \ln y = x - 3 \implies y = e^{x-3}$
So, $(g \circ f)^{-1}(x) = e^{x-3}$
Now $(g \circ f)^{-1}(a) = \sqrt{e}
\implies e^{a-3} = e^{\frac{1}{2}}
\implies a - 3 = \frac{1}{2} \text{ \{equating indices\}}
\implies a = \frac{7}{2}$
